      "Sweep lanes: a lane counts as approaching an open side when its closest point to the berth has a clear straight hull run to the berth. Lanes that instead hit the land beside the dock (e.g. head-on at over ~322 sub-units lateral offset) run aground there, some outside the reach, because the clear-path rule is unchanged; those lanes are excluded from the sweep.",
